id: pm-ts-starter-tqmv
title: Copy the sdk-contracts consumer once per bound instead of through a template
description: "CodeRabbit on #154 (PRRT_kwDOSZpwFM6xyGXo): consumer mode copies the consumer into template, then template into each bound, so node_modules is written three times when FICLONE falls back to byte copies (ext4/NTFS). Internal links are rewritten as absolute paths into each destination, so renaming template into the last bound is unsafe. Measure on a realistic consumer without clone support, then copy straight into each bound (validateDependencies + registryConfiguration per copy) or skip outDir/declarationDir/tsBuildInfo outside the parsed file list. Correctness is unaffected."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[2]: performance,sdk-contracts
